4
00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:23.000
War bonds, but backwards. The Core Problem: Good Ideas Die in Committee.

5
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:28.160
Here's your species' fun puzzle: you know how to save millions of lives.

6
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.240
You can measure exactly how many. You have the money. You don't do it.

7
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:41.220
Not because your politicians are evil. Because your system is built so that: Politicians maximize reelection, status, and

8
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:50.820
post-office careers, not "humans continuing to exist". Bureaucracies maximize budget and turf, not "speed of treatments".

9
00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:57.990
Lobbyists maximize client profits, not "global welfare". You don't fix this with awareness campaigns.

10
00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:04.739
You've been "raising awareness" for decades and everyone is still dying, but they're dying aware, so that's nice.

11
00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:10.920
You don't fix it with white papers. Politicians use white papers to stabilize wobbly tables.

12
00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:19.580
You fix it by changing WHAT SELF-INTEREST POINTS AT. On Wishonia, we used something very similar to bootstrap the whole

13
00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:23.680
transition four thousand, two hundred and ninety-seven years ago.

14
00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:30.960
We don't need them anymore (people do useful things because they're useful, which I realize sounds made up, but you also

15
00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:34.710
thought "washing your hands" sounded made up until eighteen forty-seven).

16
00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:43.540
The point is: you need them now. This chapter describes how to legally bribe your politicians into doing the right thing.

17
00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:52.040
Incentive Alignment Bonds (I.A.B.s): a financial instrument for paying for better governance without technically paying

18
00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:55.420
politicians, giving money to governments, or going to prison.

19
00:01:56.360 --> 00:02:00.700
Your one percent Treaty isn't constrained by physics, biology, or money.

20
00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:08.259
It's constrained by POLITICS, which is like being constrained by your dog's opinion on quantum mechanics, except your dog

21
00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:14.080
can veto legislation. No politician wants to be the one who "cut the military."

22
00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.820
Even by one percent. Even if that one percent cures cancer.

23
00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:22.880
The attack ads write themselves: "Senator Johnson voted to WEAKEN AMERICA."

24
00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:27.820
Your system does exactly what it's incentivized to do. It's not broken.

25
00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:36.740
It's working perfectly at the wrong thing. The fix: tell every politician on Earth, "Vote for a one percent-style reform

26
00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:42.640
and you get better reelection odds and a Goldman Sachs board seat when you retire."

27
00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:51.520
No backroom deals. No suitcases of cash. Just a standing, public rule: do the objectively good thing, and the world systematically

28
00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:58.740
rewards you. Nobody has to become a better person. The money just circulates until diseases stop existing.

29
00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:05.140
How I.A.B.s Work (Four Steps). Not charity (doesn't scale).

30
00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:11.340
Not lobbying (slot taken). Not "paying politicians" (illegal, slot also taken).

31
00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:16.280
You work with the primates you have, not the primates you wish you had.

32
00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:23.020
Step One: Pick a Measurable Outcome. Measure funding flows, not health outcomes.

33
00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:26.640
You can't attribute a treatment breakthrough to any single country's funding.

34
00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:34.400
But you CAN measure: percent of military spending redirected, total dollars contributed, and politician votes on treaty

35
00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:41.900
passage. Health improvements justify the policy. Funding flows are the scoreboard, because that's what politicians actually

36
00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:49.380
control. Step two: Raise Capital. Investors buy incentive alignment bonds, or I.A.B.s.

37
00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:55.240
Capital sits in a trust. It pays out if and only if public-good targets are hit.

38
00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:02.640
Same structure as green bonds and catastrophe bonds. Step three: Reward Your Politicians (Indirectly).

39
00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:11.080
When a politician votes for a one percent-style policy and funding actually flows: Public Good Scores rise (published by

40
00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:17.779
independent rating organizations). Electoral support increases (independent campaigns favor high-scorers).

41
00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:22.640
Post-office opportunities unlock (fellowships, boards, speaking circuits).

42
00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:26.900
No money flows to politicians (see why this isn't bribery).

43
00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:31.160
What flows is reputation, electoral advantage, and career advancement.

44
00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:39.920
Step four: Watch Self-Interest Do the Rest. Your politicians' utility function is roughly: U equals P.

45
00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:45.380
(reelection) plus career advancement plus post-office income plus legacy.

46
00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:52.980
I.A.B.s make supporting one percent-equivalent policies strictly increase all four terms.

47
00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:59.520
No altruism required. "Maximize personal payoff" and "reduce suffering" become the same action.

48
00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:04.140
You've tricked your leaders into saving lives by making it the selfish thing to do.

49
00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:13.640
The Three-Layer Architecture (How to Not Go to Prison). You cannot legally say "support Bill number X Y Z one two three

50
00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:21.060
and get paid." That's bribery. But you can create a system where politicians who support a class of pro-social policies

51
00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:29.060
systematically get more of everything they want. The trick: rule-based, universal, announced in advance.

52
00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:39.940
Layer A: Scoring (Data Only). An independent organization assigns each politician a Public Good Score based on votes, sponsorship,

53
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:43.580
and funding flows. Scores cover a policy class (any greater than or equal to one percent military-to-health reallocation),

54
00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:48.380
not a specific bill. Public, rules-based, non-partisan. (See the Senator Smith example for how scores translate to concrete

55
00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:57.740
payoffs.). Layer B: Electoral Benefits (Separate Actors). Independent PACs and five oh one c fours commit in advance to

56
00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:06.080
favor high-scoring politicians. The goal: make the Public Good Score as influential as Moody's credit ratings or N.R.A.

57
00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:06.920
grades. Moody's can downgrade a country and suddenly borrowing costs spike.

58
00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:10.060
N.R.A. grades already determine which politicians get funded.

59
00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:17.640
Same gun, different target. Layer C: Post-Office Careers (The Goldman Sachs Board Problem).

60
00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:24.760
Foundations and think tanks set eligibility rules: Public Good Score above X gets you W.H.O.

61
00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:30.960
boards and Aspen fellowships. Below X, you're explaining at dinner why you voted against curing diseases.

62
00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:37.540
The revolving door, but spinning toward "saved lives" instead of toward whoever paid the most lobbyists.

63
00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:46.920
Legal Entity Separation. For the scoring layer, a five zero one c three research organization manages metrics, dashboards,

64
00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:55.340
and public data, but cannot support or oppose candidates. For the electoral layer, a five zero one c four, PAC, or Super

65
00:06:55.340 --> 00:07:01.080
PAC makes independent expenditures for high-scorers, but cannot coordinate with candidates.

66
00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:09.380
For the post-office layer, foundations and think tanks set eligibility criteria, but cannot condition grants on specific

67
00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:16.840
votes. Three separate entities that definitely don't coordinate but somehow all reward the same behavior.

68
00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:24.640
Your species invented this structure. It's genuinely one of your better ideas, which is a low bar, but still.

69
00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:31.320
Why This Isn't Bribery. Four reasons your lawyers will stop hyperventilating: One.

70
00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:36.420
No one is paid to break a duty. "Do your job better and we'll tell everyone you did."

71
00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:43.160
That's a performance review, not a bribe. Two. Rules are universal and ex-ante.

72
00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:49.140
Same rules, all politicians, all parties, announced publicly in advance.

73
00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:54.470
No envelopes in parking garages. Three. No money goes to politicians.

74
00:07:55.040 --> 00:08:00.660
They benefit indirectly: better scores, electoral support, nicer career options.

75
00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:04.760
This is how democracy was supposed to work before your species broke it.

76
00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:10.500
Four. Scores are based on public voting records. Did they vote YES?

77
00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:17.560
Verifiable and ungameable. The ten percent fund flows automatically based on treasury inflows.

78
00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:25.800
Pure math. Bribery corrupts alignment. Incentive alignment bonds, or I.A.B.s, create it.

79
00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:34.299
Wealthy actors already buy policy (pharma spends three hundred million dollars a year on lobbying, defense contractors spend

80
00:08:34.299 --> 00:08:41.159
